{
  "id": "site.st_olaf",
  "name": "St Olaf's church",
  "name_1343": "St Olaf's (Olai kerke), parish church of the north quarter",
  "confidence": "attested church, vaults c. 1330, tower upper stage 1364+; 1343 plan reconstructed inside the surviving footprint (plausible composite)",
  "sources": [
    "history/dossiers/religion/churches-and-religious-houses.md",
    "docs/reports/st_olaf_1343_remodel.md"
  ],
  "period_notes": [
    "Rule (maintainer 2026-10-07): features dated after 1343 are left out; where the 1343 state is unrecorded, a slightly simplified form of the later, documented church is used (plausible composite).",
    "Excluded as dated later: the upper tower (1364+), the record spire (c. 1450), the basilica nave with its clerestory and star vaults and the long choir (after the 1433 fire), the Mary chapel (16th c.), the 19th-century altar, pulpit, pews and brass chandeliers.",
    "Attested for 1343: a short church with a massive west tower (walls ~3.2 m), a vaulted hall nave (vaults completed c. 1330, dated boss), a small east chancel; the tower stands unfinished.",
    "Unrecorded in 1343, simplified later form: grey limestone rubble exterior with dressed portals; a three-aisle hall of four bays on square piers with moulded imposts and pointed arches; quadripartite rib vaults with red-ochre brick ribs (the later vaults carry such ribs); lime-washed interior; two-light lancets with leaded stained glass; plank floor; oak benches; iron candle crowns; a timber pulpit; a winged retable on the high altar and side altars of the guilds at the aisle ends; the bells in a provisional timber belfry with a shingled cap on the unfinished tower, a putlog scaffold and a masons' yard."
  ],
